# `data/` ownership for Studio

Studio (PHP-FPM) runs as `www-data` and must write files under `data/` (`ui-localizations.json`, `studio-config.json`, `jobs/`, `captions/`, etc.).

## Required after any root write under `data/`

If you create or overwrite files under `data/` while running as root (Write tool, shell redirect, Python, etc.), immediately restore ownership:

```bash
chown www-data:www-data -- path/to/file
# or for multiple paths / dirs:
chown -R www-data:www-data -- data/ui-localizations.json data/studio-config.json
```

Prefer `sudo -u www-data …` when writing those files so ownership never flips.

## Why

Root-owned `644` files break Studio saves and auto-translate (`Could not open … for writing`). Default ACLs on `data/` are a safety net; ownership fix is still mandatory.
